Permit2ValidationLib::validateTokenIn
├── given mode is SKIP
│   └── it should return the pre-computed hash from calldata
├── given mode is STORAGE
│   ├── given token is whitelisted
│   │   └── it should return valid and computed hash
│   ├── given token is not whitelisted
│   │   └── it should return invalid
│   ├── given whitelist is empty
│   │   └── it should return invalid
│   ├── given multiple tokens all whitelisted
│   │   └── it should return valid and computed hash
│   └── given multiple tokens with one not whitelisted
│       └── it should return invalid
├── given mode is CATCHALL
│   ├── given token is whitelisted at chainId 0
│   │   └── it should return valid using catchall lookup
│   └── given token is only whitelisted at actual chainId
│       └── it should return invalid
└── given mode is SUBPOLICY
    ├── given subpolicy approves
    │   └── it should return valid and computed hash
    └── given subpolicy rejects
        └── it should return invalid